<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia health care stocks index to begin Sept 1.</title>
<headline>Australia health care stocks index to begin Sept 1.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Stock Exchange said on Friday  that it will launch a health care and biotechnology sector index from  September 1.</p>
<p>It said the index will consist of 11 companies with a combined market  capitalisation of A$4.98 billion.</p>
<p>The companies are involved in industries ranging from pharmaceutical,  biotechnology, hospital management, health/medical services, and therapeutic  products and services.</p>
<p>The new index replaces the miscellaneous services index with other  companies in that index to be grouped under the miscellaneous industrials  index.  </p>
<p>Companies to form the new health care and biotechnology index are  (with market capitalisation included);</p>
<p>Amrad Corp Ltd (A$243 million),</p>
<p>Australian Hospital Care Ltd (A$273 million),</p>
<p>Australian Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd (A$356 million),</p>
<p>Biota Holdings Ltd (A$305 million),</p>
<p>Cochlear Ltd (A$234 million),</p>
<p>Cortecs International Ltd (A$622 million),</p>
<p>CSL Ltd (A$1.043 billion),</p>
<p>F.H. Faulding and Co Ltd (A$1.045 billion),  </p>
<p>OPSM Protector Ltd (A$518 million),</p>
<p>Sonic Healthcare Ltd (A$222 million), and</p>
<p>Progen Industries Ltd (A$121 million).</p>
<p>The ASX said two companies involved in the sector but not included  in the index composition because they are too small are Blackmores  Ltd and Peptech Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
